WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.559 --> 00:00:02.370
(truck rumbling)

00:00:02.370 --> 00:00:03.810
- [Narrator] After months
of bloody fighting,

00:00:03.810 --> 00:00:06.880
Ukrainian soldiers at the
besieged Azovstal Steel plant

00:00:06.880 --> 00:00:07.810
laid down their arms

00:00:07.810 --> 00:00:11.250
and started being evacuated by
Russian forces as prisoners,

00:00:11.250 --> 00:00:14.109
apparently ceding control of Mariupol.

00:00:14.109 --> 00:00:17.770
(Volodymyr speaking in foreign language)

00:00:17.770 --> 00:00:19.530
- [Narrator] Soldiers
being carried out to buses

00:00:19.530 --> 00:00:20.870
could be seen in footage shared

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:23.060
by local authorities and Russian media

00:00:23.060 --> 00:00:24.640
after Russia announced an agreement

00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:25.973
for the wounded to leave.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.870
The site was the final holdout

00:00:28.870 --> 00:00:31.710
of Ukrainian soldiers who had
resisted Russia's occupation

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.410
of the strategic port city,

00:00:33.410 --> 00:00:35.210
even after Moscow declared control

00:00:35.210 --> 00:00:37.223
over Mariupol in late April.

00:00:38.240 --> 00:00:39.600
Here's how Azovstal,

00:00:39.600 --> 00:00:41.970
where hundreds of civilians
had also taken refuge

00:00:41.970 --> 00:00:44.720
for weeks, became one of
the most dramatic battles

00:00:44.720 --> 00:00:47.183
in the war, and captured
the world's attention.

00:00:48.657 --> 00:00:51.530
As the Russian army turned
Mariupol into rubble

00:00:51.530 --> 00:00:53.210
over the course of three months,

00:00:53.210 --> 00:00:56.480
it failed to quickly
seize the Azovstal plant.

00:00:56.480 --> 00:00:58.620
In a televised address last month,

00:00:58.620 --> 00:01:01.340
Putin ordered his troops to
temporarily pause the attacks

00:01:01.340 --> 00:01:03.042
and secure the area.

00:01:03.042 --> 00:01:07.640
(Vladimir speaking in foreign language)

00:01:07.640 --> 00:01:09.680
- [Narrator] The site is
a Cold War era labyrinth

00:01:09.680 --> 00:01:12.020
of warehouses, tunnels and rail tracks,

00:01:12.020 --> 00:01:14.683
spanning a territory of foursquare miles.

00:01:15.800 --> 00:01:17.940
Alongside the Azovstal fighters,

00:01:17.940 --> 00:01:20.650
hundreds of civilians got trapped.

00:01:20.650 --> 00:01:23.650
Throughout the siege, the
Ukrainian soldiers posted videos

00:01:23.650 --> 00:01:25.500
of the dire situation online,

00:01:25.500 --> 00:01:26.880
showing children and women,

00:01:26.880 --> 00:01:28.750
as well as the conditions they lived in,

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:30.884
and calling for help.

00:01:30.884 --> 00:01:35.384
(Serhiy speaking in foreign language)

00:01:44.603 --> 00:01:45.436
- [Narrator] In early May,

00:01:45.436 --> 00:01:47.340
the fighters said they were
let down by politicians

00:01:47.340 --> 00:01:50.111
and criticized Kyiv for abandoning them.

00:01:50.111 --> 00:01:54.944
(Sviatoslav speaking in foreign language)

00:02:11.664 --> 00:02:12.497
- [Narrator] The Ukrainian president

00:02:12.497 --> 00:02:14.000
had called on Russia to release

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:17.080
or exchange those remaining at Azovstal.

00:02:17.080 --> 00:02:19.890
These pleas and the worsening
humanitarian situation there

00:02:19.890 --> 00:02:21.680
got the world's attention.

00:02:21.680 --> 00:02:24.470
In late April, the UN
Secretary General met

00:02:24.470 --> 00:02:25.450
with the Russian president

00:02:25.450 --> 00:02:28.830
and asked to set up civilian
evacuations from Azovstal.

00:02:28.830 --> 00:02:29.663
Following the visit,

00:02:29.663 --> 00:02:31.370
hundreds of people were escorted out

00:02:31.370 --> 00:02:34.750
via a United Nations brokered
humanitarian corridor.

00:02:34.750 --> 00:02:37.600
But the fighters stayed on
despite dwindling prospects

00:02:37.600 --> 00:02:39.110
of a victory.

00:02:39.110 --> 00:02:40.940
The wives, girlfriends, and mothers

00:02:40.940 --> 00:02:44.120
of the Azovstal forces
lobbied for their rescue.

00:02:44.120 --> 00:02:46.500
Some embarked on an international tour,

00:02:46.500 --> 00:02:48.275
including a visit to the pope.

00:02:48.275 --> 00:02:50.760
- You are our last hope.

00:02:50.760 --> 00:02:53.120
We hope you can save their lives.

00:02:53.120 --> 00:02:55.130
Please don't let them down.

00:02:55.130 --> 00:02:58.060
- [Narrator] On Monday,
Ukraine said about 260 fighters

00:02:58.060 --> 00:02:59.940
were taken to Russian-held areas

00:02:59.940 --> 00:03:01.380
and that they will be exchanged

00:03:01.380 --> 00:03:03.400
for captured Russian soldiers

00:03:03.400 --> 00:03:06.653
while efforts continue to
evacuate remaining defenders.

00:03:07.680 --> 00:03:09.680
The Kremlin said the
soldiers would be treated

00:03:09.680 --> 00:03:12.890
in accordance with
international standards.

00:03:12.890 --> 00:03:14.490
The end of the battle for Mariupol

00:03:14.490 --> 00:03:17.510
is likely to be viewed as
a major victory in Moscow

00:03:17.510 --> 00:03:20.040
but Kyiv also called
it mission accomplished

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:22.550
as a prolonged resistance
helped the Ukrainian army

00:03:22.550 --> 00:03:24.803
to organize its resources.

00:03:24.803 --> 00:03:29.220
(Hanna speaking in foreign language)

00:03:34.747 --> 00:03:37.414
(pensive music)

